# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Ponyo's Little Library — what Git must never see
#
#  One rule matters more than all the others in this file:
#
#      THE LIBRARY IS HERS. THE CODE IS THE GIFT.
#
#  Her reading — what she finished, what she abandoned, what she wrote
#  in the margins at 2am, the photographs she attached to a memory —
#  is personal data. It belongs on her machine and in her own backups.
#  It does not belong in a repository, and absolutely not in one that
#  might one day be pushed to GitHub.
#
#  So the data rules below are deliberately wider than they need to be
#  today. As of Phase 2.0 none of those paths exist: her library lives
#  in the browser's IndexedDB, which Git cannot see. They are written in
#  advance because Phase 2 moves that data onto disk, and the moment it
#  lands the ignore rules must already be here — not added afterwards,
#  once a `git add .` has already swallowed it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── HER LIBRARY DATA — never commit ──────────────────────────────────
# The Phase 2 library root, wherever she or a future build puts it.
/library-data/
/library/
/Ponyo's Library/
/PonyoLibrary/
**/ponyo-library-data/

# The Phase 2 data files, if a library root is ever opened in-project.
# Anchored to the repo root so src/data/ and its real source files are
# untouched — those are catalogue, not confession.
/library.json
/settings.json
/covers/
/uploads/
/attachments/
/memories/
/.version

# Backups and exports. A .ponyolib is a zip of her entire library:
# every note, every rating, every uploaded photograph. This is the
# single most important line in the file.
*.ponyolib
*.ponyolib.zip
ponyo-library-*.json
ponyo-library-backup*
library-export*.json

# Raw IndexedDB dumps, if one is ever pulled out for debugging.
*.indexeddb
*.idb


# ── DEPENDENCIES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# None exist today — this app has zero dependencies and no build step,
# which is the whole reason it still runs by opening a file. If Phase 2
# brings in a toolchain, these are already covered.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions
package-lock.json.bak


# ── BUILD OUTPUT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
out/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo


# ── TAURI / DESKTOP PACKAGING (Phase 2.5) ────────────────────────────
# target/ is Rust's build directory and reaches several GB. The Tauri
# config and any Rust source are source code and stay tracked; only the
# compiled output and generated bundles are ignored.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
src-tauri/Cargo.lock.bak
*.app
*.dmg
*.msi
*.exe
*.deb
*.AppImage
!start-library.bat


# ── SIGNING KEYS AND SECRETS ─────────────────────────────────────────
# There are none today (the app has exactly one external origin, the
# public Open Library cover host, and no key of any kind). Tauri's
# updater signing keys would be the first, and they must never land.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
credentials.json
*.tauri-key


# ── TEST AND TOOLING SCRATCH ─────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/*.ps1 already write to %TEMP%\ponyo-checks and %TEMP%\ponyo-shots
# rather than into the project, so nothing here exists yet either. These
# guard the case where someone redirects that output in-tree.
/shots/
/screenshots/
/.ponyo-checks/
dom.html
dom.err
*.dump.html


# ── EDITOR AND OS NOISE ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#


# ── TEMPORARY FILES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.log
npm-debug.log*
*.pid


# ── DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED ─────────────────────────────────────────
#  assets/ponyo/*.png  — ~14 MB of her artwork, six files.
#                        Kept in Git for now, on purpose. Whether it
#                        stays, moves to Git LFS, or lives outside the
#                        repo is a decision for later; until then it is
#                        tracked, because losing it would be worse than
#                        a heavy clone.
#  src/data/covers.json — generated by tools/fetch-covers.ps1, but only
#                        after a network fetch and three passes of
#                        manual correction. It is not reproducible from
#                        source alone, so it is tracked as data.
